ADVERSARIAL round 2. Be skeptical. In round 1 you (correctly) pushed me off "2D≈L1 ceiling = mixing-always-artifacts" and told me to test Meta deghost-softmax + Jump disparity-ordered-over + a one-seam depth kill-test. I did ALL of it. Now I'm converging on a NEW conclusion and I want you to attack it hard, because I may now be in a DEFEATIST local optimum.

## What I tested since round 1 (all vision-judged by my supervisor's eye + me)
1. **Meta deghost-softmax (exact NovelView formula)** on the gray-car/BMW seam → ≈ identical to alpha-blend. Reason: the per-seam DIS optical-flow warp already aligns the band 94–97% (frac colorDiff>0.15 is only 3–6%), so deghost has almost nothing to bite on. The faint car ghost persists in BOTH alpha and deghost; neither matches L1's sharpness.
2. **Jump disparity-ordered OVER (flow-magnitude as disparity)** → near no-op (changes <1% of pixels; flow magnitude is too weak/noisy a depth proxy; 83–87% of band judged "same surface").
3. **LiDAR copy-disambiguation evidence pack (DB-12 kill-test)** → THE key result: for the doubling pixels, LiDAR decisively prefers one copy (100%), BUT straddle_frac=0.000 — the TRUE single-ego-center azimuth NEVER lies between the two rotation-only copies; both copies sit on the SAME side of LiDAR-true (because both ring cams at a seam are mounted the same side of the ego origin, so dropping their similar translations shifts both copies the same way). The winning (closest) copy's residual to LiDAR-true is median 16–21 px / p90 29–63 px = 3–4× the camera-to-camera doubling gap itself (~5 px median at 18 m). So copy-SELECTION picks the less-wrong copy but neither copy is at the correct position. (Each camera is ~2 m from the ego origin → ~20–36 px parallax at 18 m; the doubling gap is just the 21–26 cm adjacent baseline.)
4. **DrivingForward (feed-forward 3DGS, AV2-finetuned, single-ego-center)** → fuses to one center (BMW appears once) but SHREDS the near-ground + is FoV-band-limited + soft. A confidence-gated DrivingForward⊕L1 composite (use 3DGS only where internally coherent, else L1) → NEG: dark soft blotches where the 3DGS replaced clean L1; the 3DGS isn't clean enough to graft anywhere.
5. **Plane-sweep MVS in the seam band** (sweep 24 depth planes 2.5–60 m; at each, reproject BOTH cams to ego-center via the N1 projection; pick the depth with best cross-view PHOTO-CONSISTENCY |slab_i − slab_j|; that agreeing color = the de-doubled ego-center view; confidence-gate on agree<T AND a distinct cost minimum, else fall back to L1). Conservative gate (agree<18, distinct>4): fires on only 3–9% of each band (0.20% of pano) → ≈ L1 (invisible edit). LOOSENED gate (agree<32, distinct>1.5): fires on 11–28% of band (0.57% of pano) → SMEARS — the BMW rear, the area above the gray car, and the storefront all show wrong-depth-reproject distortion (vision-confirmed NEG). So conservative → ≈L1 (no benefit), aggressive → smear: the SAME depth-accuracy wall that killed E2 (sparse-LiDAR reproject). Cross-view photo-consistency on the AV2 mid-range seam is confident on <1% of band pixels.

## My emerging verdict (ATTACK THIS)
"The in-band wide-baseline near-field doubling on AV2 is depth-accuracy-bound and cannot be cleanly removed by anything I have. The three operations are: copy-SELECTION (hard_select/graphcut/single-source warp) → picks the less-wrong of two ~20px-off copies → ≈ L1; copy-MIXING (alpha/deghost/Jump-over) → blends two wrong copies → ghost; depth-REPROJECT to true (the only faithful op) → needs accurate dense depth which I cannot get cleanly: sparse LiDAR smears (E2), learned 3DGS shreds (DrivingForward), cross-view MVS is confident on <0.2% (conservative → ≈L1) or smears (aggressive). Therefore the clean deliverable is `align` (single-source warp, no color wash) ≈ L1+, and the residual textureless/occlusion doubling is the physical limit that even Google/Meta tolerate."

## Attack vectors I want you to take (be concrete, cite methods)
1. Is my verdict actually a defeatist local optimum? What CLEAN method that beats L1 am I STILL not trying? Candidates to argue for/against:
   - Global spline/mesh warp (Ceres) aligning the WHOLE overlap at the dominant depth (I only did local FB-gated warp). Would it beat L1 on the facade seams without the multi-depth residual ghosting? Worth the build?
   - Layered LDI / two-layer (fg/bg) compositing from triangulated correspondences (you mentioned layer-based stereo). Concretely how, given my evidence that selection is wrong and a single warp can't?
   - A TRAINED model — but I have NO ground-truth ERP (7 non-co-located cams, no center camera). Is there a self-supervised / photometric / cross-camera-reprojection-consistency training signal that could learn clean dense depth WITHOUT GT ERP? Or is no-GT a hard blocker?
   - Re-targeting: is "single ego-center" even the right virtual center? Each camera is ~2 m off ego-origin. Would targeting a different center (e.g., per-region nearest-camera center, or an ODS circle like Jump) make the reprojection small enough to be clean? Is L1 (rotation-only = center-at-infinity) actually the RIGHT target and I should just merge the small residual?
2. Given DrivingForward shreds and plane-sweep is confident on <0.2%, is dense depth on the mid-range AV2 seam genuinely unrecoverable, or is my plane-sweep/3DGS just under-tuned (e.g., need patch-NCC not |ΔRGB|, sub-pixel depth, bilateral-solver densification, more views/temporal)? Which ONE upgrade is most likely to flip <0.2%→useful?
3. Brutal honesty: should I STOP trying to beat L1 in-band and instead (a) ship align+E1.5 + honestly document the depth-bound residual as the contribution, or (b) commit to a multi-day learned-dense-depth build? If (b), the single highest-EV concrete next experiment?

