> **â˜… ROOT CAUSE (vision-confirmed):** view-interp computes `novel = (1âˆ’shift)Â·warp_i + shiftÂ·warp_j` = an ALPHA-BLEND (average) of two warped cameras. Where the warp is imperfect (near objects, occlusion, textureless) the average = **translucent double-image / "overlap"** â€” exactly what hard_select avoids. struct15 + E1.5-photo + obj-route stacked MORE blending â†’ worse (the user's FINAL). Gray-car zoom `VIS_align_zoom_fixed.jpg` shows view+none faint ghost on the car rear; single-source clean.
> **â˜… RESEARCH (2 web agents, source-grounded â€” Surround360 `NovelView.cpp`, Jump Â§5.5, Google Seamless SV, Zhang&Liu CVPR'14, SEAGULL ECCV'16):** **GHOST comes EXCLUSIVELY from mixing two sources at one pixel.** Production paradigm = **warp-to-ALIGN â†’ graph-cut/argmax SEAM (single source) â†’ blend ONLY low-freq colour across the thin seam**. They NEVER 50/50-blend; where they combine they use flow-magnitude/DEPTH-ordered foreground-select (Surround360 deghost-softmax `lerp(blend, flowMagSoftmax, tanh(colorDiffÂ·10))`; Jump disparity-ordered `over`). Also: "score the warp by SEAM COST, not flow-error/PSNR" (= our vision-over-metrics). Refs cached: `NovelView.cpp/.h`, `jump.pdf`, webfetch PDFs (Zhang&Liu, SEAGULL, Anguelov) in repo root.
