87:> Fit GROUND + 11 facade planes (98,981 pts). The aggregate seam-agreement NCC DID rise (near doubling band: L1 0.822 → plane **0.884**; per-pixel-E2 0.841) — **BUT that mean was dominated by large FLAT regions (sky/wall/road) and MASKED salient local breakage.**
92:> **MECHANISM / why the NCC lied:** coarse planes align the flat surfaces they model, but (a) push near-ground out of frame, and (b) CANNOT represent non-planar near objects (cars/poles) — those get displaced/sliced at the plane depth, and they are exactly the salient objects whose doubling we set out to fix. Aggregate NCC averaged the flat-region gains and hid the local object breakage. **Re-confirms the project wall: non-planar near objects straddling seams have no clean plane.**
93:> **★ LESSON (logged): aggregate NCC is NOT a sufficient gate. EVERY output must be eyeballed for lost content / sliced objects / broken seams BEFORE any POS verdict (the user's standing vision-first rule — I violated it and over-claimed POS; corrected here). The eval metric must include a content-loss + salient-object-integrity check, not just a band-NCC mean.**
