codex
**Blunt Verdict**

You are not quitting early for the shippable path. You have hit a real wall for: **same-frame, source-faithful, non-generative, true ego-center seam repair without reliable dense depth**.

But tighten the claim. Don’t say “dense depth is unrecoverable.” Say: **your current depth sources do not recover it cleanly enough**. Your `_planesweep.py` is a reasonable kill-test, but it is not a full MVS system: 24 planes, raw RGB agreement, 5x5 blur, no Census/ZNCC, no SGM/MRF, no subpixel refinement, no temporal/multi-view regularization ([`_planesweep.py`](<D:\BaiduSyncdisk\2024 to future\koi chen\experiments\Waymo2Panorama\scripts\phase3\_planesweep.py:30>), [`_planesweep.py`](<D:\BaiduSyncdisk\2024 to future\koi chen\experiments\Waymo2Panorama\scripts\phase3\_planesweep.py:67>), [`_planesweep.py`](<D:\BaiduSyncdisk\2024 to future\koi chen\experiments\Waymo2Panorama\scripts\phase3\_planesweep.py:73>)).

The strongest evidence is the LiDAR copy test: `straddle_frac=0`, and the best copy is still ~16-21 px from ego-center true. That kills copy-selection, graphcut, hard-select, and “pick the better ghost” approaches ([`progress.md`](<D:\BaiduSyncdisk\2024 to future\koi chen\experiments\Waymo2Panorama\agent\progress.md:8>), [`_kt_evidencepack.py`](<D:\BaiduSyncdisk\2024 to future\koi chen\experiments\Waymo2Panorama\scripts\phase3\_kt_evidencepack.py:166>)).

**Attack On Your Candidate Escapes**

Global spline/mesh warp: not worth a major build. Google Street View does use spline/Ceres global optimization, but they describe it as subtle overlap repair under weak constraints, not true single-center geometry; they explicitly note small overlap makes the problem under-constrained. ([research.google](https://research.google/blog/seamless-google-street-view-panoramas/)) It may improve facade seam aesthetics, but with your “true lies beyond both copies” result, it has no observed target to warp toward. It will align one wrong copy to another wrong copy.

Layered LDI / two-layer: theoretically the right class, not killed by your evidence. LDI exists exactly because single sprites/warps fail with depth variation and disocclusion; Shade et al. frame LDI as multiple depths per ray for complex nearby geometry. ([cs.cmu.edu](https://www.cs.cmu.edu/~ph/869/papers/shade98.pdf)) But concretely, this becomes “get accurate dense layered depth.” Without that, two-layer compositing just becomes smarter ghosting.

Trained model: no GT ERP is not a hard blocker. You can train by leave-one-camera-out / cross-camera reprojection with fixed calibration, sparse LiDAR, occlusion masks, and smoothness. MVSNet/MPI-style cost-volume/layered representations are the right precedent: MVSNet builds a 3D cost volume via differentiable homography warping, and MPI learns a layered representation for novel views. ([openaccess.thecvf.com](https://openaccess.thecvf.com/content_ECCV_2018/html/Yao_Yao_MVSNet_Depth_Inference_ECCV_2018_paper.html)) ([tinghuiz.github.io](https://tinghuiz.github.io/projects/mpi/)) The blocker is not supervision existence; it is engineering risk, occlusion/dynamics, and domain-specific reliability.

Retargeting: yes, this is the big reframing. A true ego-center ERP is a punishing target for a non-central 7-camera rig. `L1/align` is a valid **multi-perspective source-faithful panorama** target. Jump/ODS-style systems are not “one ego-center”; they use view interpolation and compositing, and even Google later added MVS for complex layers/occlusion. ([research.google](https://research.google/pubs/jump-virtual-reality-video/)) ([blog.google](https://blog.google/products-and-platforms/products/google-ar-vr/announcing-high-quality-stitching-jump/))

**One Upgrade Worth Testing**

If you do one more classical test, make it **regularized cost-volume depth**, not “patch NCC only”:

Census or ZNCC cost, inverse-depth/disparity labels, SGM/graph-cut smoothness, left-right/neighbor consistency, subpixel quadratic fit, edge-aware guided filtering, then ego-center z-buffer render only where confidence passes. This is the only plausible way to turn `<0.2% confident` into a useful mask without learning.

But my expectation: it may clean some facade pixels; it will not robustly fix BMW/graycar/storefront without new failures.

**What I Would Do**

Ship `align + color=none/gain + E1.5` and write the residual honestly as **depth-accuracy-bound centralization error**. Do not keep tuning copy selection or blending.

If you choose the multi-day route, the highest-EV experiment is: **overfit a strip-only Band-MPI/MVSNet on one AV2 log**, supervised by leave-one-camera-out reprojection plus sparse LiDAR, then render only the seam strip to ego-center. If it cannot beat L1 on BMW after overfitting, the learned route is not worth scaling.

So: real wall for the deliverable, not a proof of impossibility for learned dense layered depth. Your clean next move is to ship the honest L1+ result, unless the research goal specifically requires a multi-day learned depth method.


